  "scope": "state:pa",
  "title": "HB980 (2021-2022 Regular Session): In firearms and other dangerous articles, providing for report of theft or loss of firearm.",
  "urls": [
    "https://www.legis.state.pa.us/cfdocs/billinfo/bill_history.cfm?syear=2021&sind=0&body=H&type=B&bn=980",
    "https://www.legis.state.pa.us/cfdocs/legis/PN/Public/btCheck.cfm?txtType=PDF&sessYr=2021&sessInd=0&billBody=H&billTyp=B&billNbr=0980&pn=0992"
  ],
  "version": "as-filed",
  "operative_text": "Sec. 1 (adding 18 Pa.C.S. 6115.1(a)): An owner or other person lawfully in possession of a firearm who suffers the loss or theft of a firearm shall, within 72 hours of the discovery of the loss or theft, report the facts and circumstances of the loss or theft to the municipal police of the jurisdiction in which the loss or theft is believed to have occurred or the Pennsylvania State Police.\nSec. 1 (adding 18 Pa.C.S. 6115.1(b)): A law enforcement agency that receives a report under this section shall, within 24 hours of receiving the report, forward notice of the loss or theft as well as all information obtained under subsection (a) to the Pennsylvania State Police.\nSec. 1 (adding 18 Pa.C.S. 6115.1(e)): Notwithstanding any other provision of law, a person who violates subsection (a) commits: (1) A summary offense for the first offense, punishable by a fine of not more than $500. (2) A misdemeanor of the second degree for a second offense. (3) A misdemeanor of the first degree for a third or subsequent offense.",
